      "writtenOn": "2025-09-09T15:06:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ryan will provide specific guidance on how to work around this one.\n\nYea, it can\u0027t be out of range, but the unsafe-buffer-usage warning in clang typically fires when you do this kind pointer arithmetic and then write into the pointer because it doesn\u0027t _know_ for sure that everything is in bounds. (In general it doesn\u0027t like things like memcpy, etc. I believe)\n\nRyan will either have slightly different code for the assignment, or will give you the macros to use to suppress the warning.",
      "parentUuid": "078bf890_f6b4f5a8",
      "revId": "e63afc0f95ffaf9a10a6040bce2456a87e4d302d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7876db5_940f6acd",
        "filename": "src/tint/cmd/common/helper.h",
